#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""ot-merge-queue: automated merge queue for main (MERGE-QUEUE-1, OWNER order 2026-11-14; replaces the hand-run ROOT-MERGE lane).

Run every 5 minutes by the systemd user timer ot-merge-queue.timer on the hub (intel2). One tick:
  1. read the review queue (~/coord/lanes/COORD-REVIEW-QUEUE.md) for sha-pinned approvals
        COORD APPROVED: <branch> @<sha>            (several per line allowed; the branch may be left out: "COORD APPROVED: @<sha>")
        COORD REVOKED: <branch> @<sha>             (cancels an approval that has not landed yet)
     only on a line written by COORD / OWNER (first [author] tag COORD or OWNER, or no tag); a lane quoting the line is ignored
  2. skip every approval already in the state file (~/merge-queue/state.json), so a tick is idempotent;
  3. for each new approval, in parallel, in its own scratch worktree of the queue clone: fetch the sha (GitHub first, then the
     hub checkout, read-only), apply it onto current main (a no-ff merge when every commit of the branch is new; cherry-pick -x of
     only the new commits when the branch also carries rebased copies of commits main already has), check that the changed
     Python/shell files parse, pick the tests from the touched paths (select_tests) and run them with pytest-xdist.  A test that
     also fails on main is baseline, not the branch's;
  4. land serially in approval order: push the tip to main (never forced), tag flow-<date>-<xx>-{head,qc,kv,s81,hbm}, post a
     MERGED line.  When main moved after the test the change is applied again; it is re-tested only when the files main changed
     overlap the files the branch changes (a textual conflict is a MERGE-FAIL);
  5. a conflict, red tests or a sha that cannot be fetched (after MQ_WAIT_TICKS ticks) -> one MERGE-FAIL line addressed to the
     branch's lane (from its READY line) naming the conflict files or the failing tests; the approval is skipped;
  6. after a push, the sync hook (MQ_SYNC_HOOK, default ot-tools-sync) materializes main@sha as the pinned tools tree rt/<sha>.
Log ~/merge-queue/log; lock ~/merge-queue/lock (a tick that finds it held exits 0).

usage: ot-merge-queue [tick] [--dry-run] [--only SHA] | ot-merge-queue status | ot-merge-queue parse
"""
